Work는 코드 제출과 검토를 최적화하여 안전하고 신뢰할 수 있는 코드를 제출하는 기술","es":"Commit-work es una herramienta de AI que ayuda a los desarrolladores a crear commits de alta calidad","fr":"Commit-work est un outil d''IA qui aide les développeurs à créer des commits de haute qualité","de":"Commit-work ist ein AI-Tool, das Entwicklern hilft, Commits von hoher Qualität zu erstellen","pt":"O Commit-Work é uma ferramenta que ajuda a criar commits de forma lógica e segura, utilizando Conventional Commits.","ru":"Commit-Work - это инструмент, который помогает создавать коммиты логичным и безопасным образом, используя Conventional Commits.","ar":"Commit-Work هو أداة تساعد في إنشاء إلتزامات بشكل منطقي وأمن، باستخدام Conventional Commits."},"features":{"en":["Ensures only intended changes are included in commits","Supports logically scoped commits with optional splitting","Enforces Conventional Commits style for commit messages","Allows specification of commit style, including max subject length and required scopes","Provides a workflow checklist for commit creation"],"zh":["仅包含预期的变化","逻辑上分割的提交","描述变更的提交消息","支持 Conventional Commits","自定义提交样式"],"ja":["予期された変更のみを含む","論理的に分割されたコミット","変更の説明を含むコミットメッセージ","Conventional Commits をサポート","カスタムコミットスタイル"],"ko":["예상된 변경만 포함","논리적으로 분할된 커밋","변경 사항을 설명하는 커밋 메시지","Conventional Commits 지원","사용자 정의 커밋 스타일"],"es":["Commits lógicamente separados para una revisión fácil","Mensajes de commit descriptivos para una mejor comprensión","Soporte para Commits Convencionales","Opción para commits individuales o múltiples","Reglas personalizables para commits, como longitud máxima de asunto y ámbitos requeridos"],"fr":["Commits logiquement séparés pour une révision facile","Messages de commit descriptifs pour une meilleure compréhension","Prise en charge des Commits Convencionales","Option pour les commits individuels ou multiples","Règles personnalisables pour les commits, comme la longueur maximale du sujet et les étendues requises"],"de":["Logisch getrennte Commits für eine einfache Überprüfung","Beschreibende Commit-Nachrichten für ein besseres Verständnis","Unterstützung für Conventional Commits","Option für einzelne oder multiple Commits","Anpassbare Regeln für Commits, wie maximale Betrefflänge und erforderliche Bereiche"],"pt":["Criação de commits lógicos e seguros","Uso de Conventional Commits","Suporte a commits únicos ou múltiplos","Otimização para revisão e envio","Compatibilidade com regras de commit personalizadas","Integração com fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Создание логичных и безопасных коммитов","Использование Conventional Commits","Поддержка единичных или множественных коммитов","Оптимизация для проверки и отправки","Совместимость с пользовательскими правилами коммита","Интеграция с рабочими процессами разработки"],"ar":["إنشاء إلتزامات منطقية وأمنة","استخدام Conventional Commits","دعم إلتزامات فردية أو متعددة","تحسين الإلتزامات للمراجعة والنشر","توافق مع قواعد الإلتزام المخصصة","تكامل مع سير عمل التطوير"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use commit-work","what is commit-work","commit-work alternative","commit-work vs git","commit-work setup guide","conventional commits tutorial","commit-work install","safe and reviewable commits"],"zh":["Commit Work","代码提交","代码审查","Conventional Commits","AIエージェント","代码优化","安全提交"],"ja":["Commit Work","コードレビュー","コード提交","Conventional Commits","AIエージェント","コード最適化","安全な_ship"],"ko":["Commit Work","코드 제출","코드 검토","Conventional Commits","AI 에이전트","코드 최적화","안전한 배포"],"es":["commit-work","herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","commit de alta calidad","commits convencionales","revisión de código","seguridad de commits","mejores prácticas para commits","desarrollo de software","control de versiones"],"fr":["commit-work","outils d''IA pour développeurs","commit de haute qualité","commits convencionales","révision de code","sécurité des commits","bonnes pratiques pour les commits","développement de logiciels","contrôle de versions"],"de":["commit-work","AI-Tools für Entwickler","Commits von hoher Qualität","Conventional Commits","Code-Überprüfung","Sicherheit von Commits","Best Practices für Commits","Software-Entwicklung","Versionskontrolle"],"pt":["Commit-Work","Conventional Commits","commits seguros","revisão de commits","melhores práticas de commit","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Índice de commit","Commit-Work GUI"],"ru":["Commit-Work","Conventional Commits","безопасные коммиты","проверка коммитов","лучшие практики коммита","инструменты разработки","Индекс коммитов","Commit-Work ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["Commit-Work","Conventional Commits","إلتزامات أمنة","مراجعة الإلتزامات","أفضل الممارسات للإلتزام","أدوات التطوير","فهرس الإلتزام","Commit-Work أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي"]}},"owner":"Neko-Protocol","repo":"Neko-DApp","repoPath":"Neko-Protocol/Neko-DApp","stars":2,"forks":16,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T02:32:30Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit-work","description":"Create high-quality git commits: review/stage intended changes, split into logical commits, and write clear commit messages (including Conventional Commits). Use when the user asks to commit, craft a commit message, stage changes, or split work into multiple commits.","bodyPreview":"# Commit work\n\n## Goal\n\nMake commits that are easy to review and safe to ship:\n\n- only intended changes are included\n- commits are logically scoped (split when needed)\n- commit messages describe what changed and why\n\n## Inputs to ask for (if missing)\n\n- Single commit or multiple commits? (If unsure: default to multiple small commits when there are unrelated changes.)\n- Commit style: Conventional Commits are required.\n- Any rules: max subject length, required scopes.\n\n## Workflow (checklist)\n\n1.","body":"# Commit work\n\n## Goal\n\nMake commits that are easy to review and safe to ship:\n\n- only intended changes are included\n- commits are logically scoped (split when needed)\n- commit messages describe what changed and why\n\n## Inputs to ask for (if missing)\n\n- Single commit or multiple commits? (If unsure: default to multiple small commits when there are unrelated changes.)\n- Commit style: Conventional Commits are required.\n- Any rules: max subject length, required scopes.\n\n## Workflow (checklist)\n\n1. Inspect the working tree before staging\n   - `git status`\n   - `git diff` (unstaged)\n   - If many changes: `git diff --stat`\n2. Decide commit boundaries (split if needed)\n   - Split by: feature vs refactor, backend vs frontend, formatting vs logic, tests vs prod code, dependency bumps vs behavior changes.\n   - If changes are mixed in one file, plan to use patch staging.\n3. Stage only what belongs in the next commit\n   - Prefer patch staging for mixed changes: `git add -p`\n   - To unstage a hunk/file: `git restore --staged -p` or `git restore --staged <path>`\n4. Review what will actually be committed\n   - `git diff --cached`\n   - Sanity checks:\n     - no secrets or tokens\n     - no accidental debug logging\n     - no unrelated formatting churn\n5. Describe the staged change in 1-2 sentences (before writing the message)\n   - \"What changed?\" + \"Why?\"\n   - If you cannot describe it cleanly, the commit is probably too big or mixed; go back to step 2.\n6. Write the commit message\n   - Use Conventional Commits (required):\n     - `type(scope): short summary`\n     - blank line\n     - body (what/why, not implementation diary)\n     - footer (BREAKING CHANGE) if needed\n   - Prefer an editor for multi-line messages: `git commit -v`\n   - Use `references/commit-message-template.md` if helpful.\n7. Run the smallest relevant verification\n   - Run the repo''s fastest meaningful check (unit tests, lint, or build) before moving on.\n8. Repeat for the next commit until the working tree is clean\n\n## Deliverable\n\nProvide:\n\n- the final commit message(s)\n- a short summary per commit (what/why)\n- the commands used to stage/review (at minimum: `git diff --cached`, plus any tests run)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T07:08:44.623Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Collaborative Development Agents requiring standardized commit formatting and review safety","zh":"适合需要标准化提交格式和审查安全的协作开发代理","ja":"標準化されたコミット形式とレビューセキュリティが必要な共同開発エージェントに最適","ko":"표준화된 커밋 형식과 리뷰 보안이 필요한 협력 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo Colaborativo que requieren un formato de confirmación estandarizado y seguridad de revisión","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développement Collaboratif nécessitant un format de validation standardisé et une sécurité de révision","de":"Ideal für Collaborative Development Agents, die ein standardisiertes Commit-Formatting und eine Überprüfungssicherheit erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Colaborativo que exigem formatação de commit padronizada e segurança de revisão","ru":"Идеально подходит для Сотрудничества Развития Агентов, требующих стандартизированного форматирования коммитов и безопасности обзора","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير التعاوني الذين يتطلبون تنسيق إلتزام موحد وأمان استعراض"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create logically scoped commits following Conventional Commits standards, ensuring easy review and safe shipping with features like commit message description and scoped changes, utilizing protocols such as Git and adhering to specific commit styles and rules like max subject length and required scopes","zh":"赋予代理创建逻辑作用域的提交，遵循Conventional Commits标准，确保易于审查和安全发布，具有提交消息描述和作用域更改等功能，利用Git等协议，遵守特定的提交样式和规则，如最大主题长度和所需作用域","ja":"エージェントがConventional Commits標準に従って論理的にスコープされたコミットを作成できるようにし、コミットメッセージの説明やスコープ変更などの機能により、レビューが容易で安全な出荷を可能にし、Gitなどのプロトコルを利用し、最大サブジェクト長や必要なスコープなどの特定のコミットスタイルやルールに従う","ko":"에이전트가 Conventional Commits 표준을 따르는 논리적으로 범위가 지정된 커밋을 생성할 수 있도록 하여 커밋 메시지 설명 및 범위 변경 등의 기능을 통해 리뷰가 쉽고 안전한 출하를 가능하게 하며 Git 등의 프로토콜을 사용하며 최대 주제 길이 및 필요한 범위 등 특정 커밋 스타일 및 규칙을遵守","es":"Permite a los agentes crear commits con ámbito lógico siguiendo los estándares de Conventional Commits, asegurando una revisión sencilla y un envío seguro con características como la descripción del mensaje de confirmación y los cambios con ámbito, utilizando protocolos como Git y ajustándose a estilos y reglas de confirmación específicos como la longitud máxima del asunto y los ámbitos requeridos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des commits à portée logique suivant les normes de Conventional Commits, assurant une révision facile et un envoi sécurisé avec des fonctionnalités comme la description du message de validation et les modifications à portée, en utilisant des protocoles tels que Git et en respectant des styles et des règles de validation spécifiques comme la longueur maximale du sujet et les portées requises","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, logisch abgegrenzte Commits nach Conventional Commits-Standards zu erstellen, wodurch eine einfache Überprüfung und ein sicheres Versenden mit Funktionen wie der Beschreibung der Commit-Meldung und den abgegrenzten Änderungen gewährleistet wird, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie Git und unter Einhaltung spezifischer Commit-Stile und -Regeln wie der maximalen Betrefflänge und der erforderlichen Bereiche","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar commits com escopo lógico seguindo os padrões Conventional Commits, garantindo fácil revisão e envio seguro com recursos como descrição de mensagem de commit e alterações com escopo, utilizando protocolos como Git e aderindo a estilos e regras de commit específicos, como comprimento máximo de assunto e escopos obrigatórios","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать логически определенные коммиты, следуя стандартам Conventional Commits, обеспечивая легкий обзор и безопасную доставку с функциями, такими как описание сообщения коммита и изменений с областью, используя протоколы, такие как Git, и соблюдая определенные стили и правила коммитов, такие как максимальная длина темы и обязательные области","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء إلتزامات ذات نطاق منطقي تتبع معايير الالتزامات التقليدية، مما يضمن استعراضًا سهلًا وتسليمًا آمنًا مع ميزات مثل وصف رسالة الإلتزام والتغييرات المحددة النطاق، وتستخدم بروتوكولات مثل Git وملتزمه بأسلوب إلتزام معين وقواعد مثل أقصى طول موضوع والمناطقة المطلوبة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit creation for collaborative projects","Generating commit messages that describe changes and reasons","Splitting large commits into smaller, logically scoped ones"],"zh":["为协作项目自动创建提交","生成描述更改和原因的提交消息","将大型提交拆分为较小、逻辑作用域的提交"],"ja":["共同開発プロジェクトのためのコミット自動生成","変更と理由を記述したコミットメッセージの生成","大きなコミットを小さな論理的にスコープされたコミットに分割"],"ko":["협력 프로젝트를 위한 커밋 자동 생성","변경 및 이유를 설명하는 커밋 메시지 생성","큰 커밋을 작은 논리적으로 범위가 지정된 커밋으로 분할"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de confirmaciones para proyectos colaborativos","Generación de mensajes de confirmación que describen los cambios y los motivos","División de confirmaciones grandes en otras más pequeñas y con ámbito lógico"],"fr":["Automation de la création de validations pour les projets collaboratifs","Génération de messages de validation qui décrivent les modifications et les raisons","Scission de validations importantes en de plus petites et à portée logique"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von Commits für kollaborative Projekte","Erzeugung von Commit-Meldungen, die die Änderungen und Gründe beschreiben","Aufteilung großer Commits in kleinere, logisch abgegrenzte"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de commits para projetos colaborativos","Gerar mensagens de commit que descrevam alterações e motivos","Dividir commits grandes em menores, com escopo lógico"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание коммитов для совместных проектов","Генерировать сообщения коммитов, которые описывают изменения и причины","Разделить большие коммиты на меньшие, логически определенные"],"ar":["تحسين proceso自動ي لإنشاء الإلتزامات لمشاريع تعاونية","توليد رسائل إلتزام تصف التغييرات والأسباب","تقسيم الإلتزامات الكبيرة إلى صغيرة، ذات نطاق منطقي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to Conventional Commits standards","Limited to Git version control system","May require additional configuration for custom commit styles or rules"],"zh":["需要遵守Conventional Commits标准","仅限于Git版本控制系统","可能需要为自定义提交样式或规则进行额外配置"],"ja":["Conventional Commits標準の遵守が必要","Gitバージョン管理システムに限定","カスタムコミットスタイルまたはルールには追加の設定が必要となる場合がある"],"ko":["Conventional Commits 표준을遵守해야 함","Git 버전 관리 시스템에만 국한","사용자 정의 커밋 스타일 또는 규칙에는 추가 구성이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la adherencia a los estándares de Conventional Commits","Limitado al sistema de control de versiones Git","Puede requerir una configuración adicional para estilos o reglas de confirmación personalizados"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion aux normes de Conventional Commits","Limité au système de contrôle de version Git","Peut nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire pour les styles ou les règles de validation personnalisés"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der Conventional Commits-Standards","Begrenzt auf das Git-Versionskontrollsystem","Kann eine zusätzliche Konfiguration für benutzerdefinierte Commit-Stile oder -Regeln erfordern"],"pt":["Exige aderência aos padrões Conventional Commits","Limitado ao sistema de controle de versão Git","Pode exigir configuração adicional para estilos ou regras de commit personalizados"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения стандартов Conventional Commits","Ограничен системой контроля версий Git","Может потребовать дополнительной настройки для пользовательских стилей или правил коммитов"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بمعايير الالتزامات التقليدية","محدود بنظام التحكم في الإصدار Git","قد يتطلب تكوينًا إضافيًا لأسلوب أو قواعد إلتزام مخصصة"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"369786c13587086f6d052256a9fd4a1cdcb4173952b5bc9ce15afce9f0aeb00a","qualityScore":41}');
